  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Kepler&#39;s Third Law &ndash; The Law of Periods,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math><br /><br />where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is time taken by the planet to go once around the sun and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the semi-major axis (distance) of the elliptical orbit.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8230;</mo></math>(i)<br /><br />Where <math><mi>k</mi></math> is a constant of proportionality.<br /><br />When <math><mi>R</mi></math> becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times, let the time period be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfenced></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mfenced><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />So, time period will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>yr</mi></math>.",
